eighted_loss": false, "epoch": 7}}, {"seed": 2, "dev_wf1": 48.4, "test_wf1": 50.05, "settings": {"weighted_loss": false, "epoch": 2}}], "dev_wf1_mean": 48.68, "dev_wf1_std": 0.63, "test_wf1_mean": 50.27, "test_wf1_std": 0.34}}, "gain": {"logreg": -1.35, "mlp_mean": -0.91, "mlp_std": 0.94}}}, "last_night_mlp_test_wf1": 61.36, "best_vision_by_dev": "qwen3.5-4b/reader", "notes": "One line at a time with no dialogue context. Logistic regression runs once; the MLP runs with seeds 0, 1, 2 and is reported as the mean and sample standard deviation over them; seed 0 is the seed last night's single run used. The whisper rows train, tune and test on Whisper's transcripts of the clips, the words the live demo reads; completed rows use MELD's published words. Vision sets miss clips whose frames failed to extract, so a joined row drops those clips from train, dev and test alike; each joined row is therefore compared with the text-only heads trained and scored on exactly the same clips, and the gain is the difference. The gain's standard deviation is the square root of the sum of both rows' squared seed standard deviations, and a gain smaller than about two of those is not a real difference. Face-view rows end with a has_face column, 1.0 when a face was found in any frame and 0.0 when the row is all zeros. The best vision set for the all-three row is picked by mean dev MLP F1."}
